<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>ReBooty Ops — eBay Sync</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css?v=<%= cssVersion %>">
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>eBay Sync</h1>
    <%- include('../partials/nav') %>

    <p>Pulls your current eBay listings and recent orders into the app. This can take a
      minute or two for a full sync — the page will just sit and load until it's done,
      that's normal.</p>

    <form method="POST" action="/sync/run">
      <button type="submit">Run Sync Now</button>
    </form>

    <% if (error) { %>
      <div class="error" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Sync failed: <%= error %></div>
    <% } %>

    <p style="margin-top:1rem;"><a href="/sync/diagnose">Run network diagnostic</a> (for the Hostinger support ticket, if sync is failing with a 500 from the token endpoint)</p>

    <% if (result) { %>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <strong>Listings</strong>
        <div><%= result.listings.totalListings %> active checked</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.created %> new</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.updated %> updated</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.matchedBySku %> matched by SKU</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.binLocationBackfilled %> bin/loc backfilled</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.endedOutOfStock %> moved to Ended (out of stock)</div>
        <div><%= result.listings.endedMissing %> moved to Ended (gone from eBay)</div>
        <% if (result.listings.duplicateCustomLabels > 0) { %>
          <div style="color:#c53030;"><%= result.listings.duplicateCustomLabels %> duplicate Custom Label(s) found on eBay -- a new SKU was generated instead. Check eBay for a copied/relisted item carrying a stale label.</div>
        <% } %>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <strong>Orders</strong>
        <div><%= result.orders.totalOrders %> checked</div>
        <div><%= result.orders.newSales %> new sales</div>
        <div><%= result.orders.updatedSales %> updated</div>
        <div><%= result.orders.backfilledInventory %> inventory rows backfilled</div>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <hr style="margin:2rem 0;">

    <h2>Backfill Old Orders</h2>
    <p>The regular sync above only checks the last few days of eBay orders, to stay
      fast. If an item looks stuck (e.g. shows up in <a href="/inventory/ended">Ended</a>
      but you suspect it actually sold on eBay a while back), run this with a wider
      date range to check further back — it uses the exact same order-matching logic,
      just over more days. Nothing on eBay's side is touched either way; this only
      reads eBay orders and updates our own inventory/sales records.</p>

    <form method="POST" action="/sync/backfill-orders">
      <label for="days">Look back this many days</label>
      <input type="number" id="days" name="days" value="90" min="1" max="730">
      <button type="submit">Backfill Orders</button>
    </form>

    <% if (backfillResult) { %>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <strong>Order backfill (<%= backfillResult.days %> days)</strong>
        <div><%= backfillResult.totalOrders %> checked</div>
        <div><%= backfillResult.newSales %> new sales</div>
        <div><%= backfillResult.updatedSales %> updated</div>
        <div><%= backfillResult.backfilledInventory %> inventory rows backfilled</div>
        <div><%= backfillResult.markedShipped %> marked shipped</div>
      </div>
    <% } %>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
